# implements-port slice 11 (B2; Q43 -- a cell of `rows:` is an argument, delimited as any actual list is):
# unit_s7_prim_cross over its own convert.lm2 whose second row has the cell `0 + 0`
# (tests/unit_s7_conv_cellexpr_table.lm2): one cell, the rows stay aligned, Entry 7.  Before, its three atoms
# were three cells and the rows were refused as not whole.
fn: go () int
    int: a 1
    size_t: b 2U
    a: b
    return: a

int: k
k: go()
if: k = 2
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 1; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
